correction.prompt:
You are correcting invalid grounded RDF statements produced by another extraction agent.

Return the same extraction JSON schema used by the original extraction agent.

Source unit ID: u_6e72b551c87fe993d8b736b1d4fed8d689fe3467b8a790558c6c9e44435994e2
Title: Chaim Herzog
Text:
Major-General Chaim Herzog (; 17 September 1918 – 17 April 1997) was an Israeli politician, general, lawyer and author who served as the sixth President of Israel between 1983 and 1993. Born in Belfast and raised predominantly in Dublin, the son of Ireland's Chief Rabbi Yitzhak HaLevi Herzog, he emigrated to Mandatory Palestine in 1935 and served in the Haganah Jewish paramilitary group during the 1936–39 Arab revolt. In the British Army during World War II, latterly as an officer, he received the nickname "Vivian" because the British could not pronounce "Chaim". He returned to Palestine after the war and, following the end of the British Mandate and Israel's Declaration of Independence in 1948, operated in the battles for Latrun during the 1948 Arab–Israeli War. He retired from the Israel Defence Forces in 1962 with the rank of Major-General.

Rejected statements and validator errors:
[
  {
    "statement_index": 16,
    "statement": {
      "subject": {
        "value": "Chaim Herzog",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "segment": "title",
            "quote": "Chaim Herzog",
            "occurrence": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      "predicate": {
        "value": "servedIn",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "segment": "text",
            "quote": "served in the British Army",
            "occurrence": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      "object": {
        "value": "British Army",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "segment": "text",
            "quote": "British Army",
            "occurrence": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "validator_error": "response.statements[16].predicate.evidence[0]: quote 'served in the British Army' does not occur in source segment 'text'"
  }
]

Correction rules:
- Return only corrected replacements for the rejected statements.
- Do not repeat statements that were already valid.
- Every evidence quote must occur verbatim in the declared title or text segment.
- Use the correct 1-based occurrence of each evidence quote.
- Keep a statement only when its semantic claim is supported by the source.
- Omit a statement when it cannot be corrected without inventing evidence or meaning.
- Do not add unrelated statements or facts.

Return exactly one JSON object:
{
  "statements": [
    {
      "subject": {"value": "...", "evidence": [...]},
      "predicate": {"value": "...", "evidence": [...]},
      "object": {"value": "...", "evidence": [...]}
    }
  ]
}

Object datatype is optional and uses the same original extraction contract.
Do not return Markdown fences, commentary, repair actions, indices, or additional fields.

